{
  "bases": [
    "express-esm"
  ],
  "modules": [
    {
      "key": "auth-jwt",
      "name": "JWT Auth",
      "dimension": "auth",
      "dependsOn": [
        "db-mongoose"
      ],
      "languages": [
        "esm"
      ],
      "esm": {
        "dependencies": {
          "jsonwebtoken": "^9.0.2",
          "bcryptjs": "^2.4.3",
          "cookie-parser": "^1.4.6",
          "zod": "^3.23.8"
        },
        "devDependencies": {},
        "envExample": [
          "",
          "# Use long, random values in production (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`)",
          "JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-access-secret",
          "JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-refresh-secret",
          "JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN=15m",
          "JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN=7d"
        ],
        "wiring": {
          "app": {
            "imports": [
              "import cookieParser from \"cookie-parser\";"
            ],
            "middleware": [
              "app.use(cookieParser());"
            ]
          },
          "routes/index": {
            "imports": [
              "import authRoutes from \"../routes/auth.routes.js\";"
            ],
            "mounts": [
              "router.use(\"/auth\", authRoutes);"
            ]
          },
          "test/setup": {
            "env": [
              "process.env.JWT_ACCESS_SECRET ||= \"test-access-secret\";",
              "process.env.JWT_REFRESH_SECRET ||= \"test-refresh-secret\";"
            ]
          }
        },
        "readme": "\n## Auth\n\nJWT access token (short-lived, returned in the response body) + refresh token (long-lived, httpOnly cookie).\n\n- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` — create an account\n- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` — get a new access token + refresh cookie\n- `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` — exchange the refresh cookie for a new access token\n- `POST /api/v1/auth/logout` — clears the refresh cookie\n- `GET /api/v1/auth/me` — current user (requires `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`)\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "db-mongoose",
      "name": "MongoDB + Mongoose",
      "dimension": "database",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "languages": [
        "esm"
      ],
      "esm": {
        "dependencies": {
          "mongoose": "^8.4.1"
        },
        "devDependencies": {
          "mongodb-memory-server": "^10.0.0"
        },
        "envExample": [
          "MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/{{projectName}}"
        ],
        "wiring": {
          "server": {
            "imports": [
              "import { connectDB } from \"./config/db.js\";"
            ],
            "startup": [
              "await connectDB();"
            ]
          },
          "test/setup": {
            "imports": [
              "import mongoose from \"mongoose\";",
              "import { MongoMemoryServer } from \"mongodb-memory-server\";"
            ],
            "state": [
              "let mongoServer;"
            ],
            "beforeAll": [
              "mongoServer = await MongoMemoryServer.create();",
              "const mongoUri = mongoServer.getUri();",
              "process.env.MONGO_URI = mongoUri;",
              "await mongoose.connect(mongoUri);"
            ],
            "afterAll": [
              "await mongoose.disconnect();",
              "await mongoServer.stop();"
            ]
          }
        },
        "readme": "\n## Database\n\nMongoDB via Mongoose. Set `MONGO_URI` in `.env` (defaults to a local instance on 27017). Note: `mongodb-memory-server` is included so tests can run against a real in-memory MongoDB without a local install, whether or not you also picked the testing module.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "rbac-permission",
      "name": "Permission-based RBAC",
      "dimension": "rbac",
      "dependsOn": [
        "auth-jwt"
      ],
      "languages": [
        "esm"
      ],
      "esm": {
        "dependencies": {},
        "devDependencies": {},
        "wiring": {
          "routes/index": {
            "imports": [
              "import adminRoutes from \"../routes/admin.routes.js\";"
            ],
            "mounts": [
              "router.use(\"/\", adminRoutes);"
            ]
          }
        },
        "readme": "\n## RBAC (Permission-based)\n\nA role maps to a list of permissions in `config/permissions.js`, and routes declare which permission they need:\n\n```js\nrouter.get(\"/admin-check\", requireAuth, requirePermission(\"admin:access\"), handler);\n```\n\nAdd a new role, or change what an existing role can do, by editing `config/permissions.js` only. See `routes/admin.routes.js` for a working example (`GET /api/v1/admin-check`).\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "rbac-simple",
      "name": "Simple Role RBAC",
      "dimension": "rbac",
      "dependsOn": [
        "auth-jwt"
      ],
      "languages": [
        "esm"
      ],
      "esm": {
        "dependencies": {},
        "devDependencies": {},
        "wiring": {
          "routes/index": {
            "imports": [
              "import adminRoutes from \"../routes/admin.routes.js\";"
            ],
            "mounts": [
              "router.use(\"/\", adminRoutes);"
            ]
          }
        },
        "readme": "\n## RBAC (Simple)\n\nEach user has one `role`: `\"user\"` or `\"admin\"`. Protect a route with:\n\n```js\nrouter.get(\"/admin-check\", requireAuth, requireRole(\"admin\"), handler);\n```\n\nSee `routes/admin.routes.js` for a working example (`GET /api/v1/admin-check`).\n"
      }
    },
    {
